  "rationale": "Setting both --trunclenf 230 and --trunclenr 180 passes validation and sets find_truncation_values to false, so the automatic TRUNCLEN step no longer runs. The fixed cutoffs go straight into DADA2_FILTNTRIM, which changes the filtered reads and therefore every ASV-dependent step after it: denoising, the post-processing filters, taxonomy classification, the QIIME2 downstream analyses, the R objects, the summary tables and the reports. Steps that come before filtering or only process reference databases or metadata are unchanged: FastQC, cutadapt, DADA2_QUALITY1, FORMAT_TAXONOMY, CUTADAPT_TAXONOMY, QIIME2_PREPTAX and the METADATA_* steps."
